# Wireless CSI ingest (TCP 9055) — keep in mind

**Status (Sep 2026):** Working end-to-end. Multi-C5 TCP fan-in supported on `:9055`.

## Architecture

```
LabPSK AP --CSI--> ESP32-C5 #1 ──TCP :9055──┐
           ├─CSI--> ESP32-C5 #2 ──TCP :9055──┼──► Mac Mini (run_ingest) --> Postgres
           └─CSI--> ESP32-C5 #3 ──TCP :9055──┘     samples.source_id = client IP
```

Lab room 207: **three** wall-powered C5 receivers (method 4.1), same AP, one Mini ingest. Add more the same way (backlog=8).

- Firmware: `esp-csi/examples/get-started/csi_recv_router` (`csi_tcp_forward.c`, Kconfig `CSI_TCP_*`)
- Flash each board: `CSI_TCP_HOST=<mini_ip> ./scripts/set_csi_wifi.sh …` (same Mini IP on all)
- Ingest: `csi_pipeline_new/./run_multi_ingest.sh` (or `./run_ingest.sh --listen-tcp 9055 …`)
- Docs: `csi_pipeline_new/README.md` (Wireless CSI over TCP) + `MAC_MINI.md`

**Ops model:** flash each C5 once (`CSI_TCP_HOST=<mini_ip>`). Whenever Mini runs multi-ingest, **every powered board** that can reach `:9055` fans in automatically; no per-board start step. One board down does not stop ingest from the rest.
