## Remote control

- **Office laptop → Mini SSH works** (use this for start/stop/monitor)
- **LabPSK Wi‑Fi clients** (personal Mac on LabPSK) often **cannot** ping/SSH Mini (client isolation) even when C5→Mini TCP works
- Prefer `tmux` on Mini for long runs; monitor via ingest logs (`inserted total=…`) or Postgres counts

## Correct / good enough (lab capture)

- TCP (not UDP) for long CSI lines
- Heap-backed send queue (fixed prior stack overflow in `csi_tcp` task)
- USB serial print still works alongside TCP
- **Multi-C5:** one `--listen-tcp 9055` accepts many boards; `csi_samples.source_id` = client IP
- **One board down ≠ ingest down:** each C5 has its own TCP reader thread; disconnect only drops that client (`active` decreases). Others keep inserting; acceptor stays up for reconnect. Idle warn is per-`source_id` when some are still live.
- **Run until Ctrl+C:** no firmware time limit; watchdog keeps CSI/TCP alive for long sessions
- **Target ping rate:** 100 Hz (`CONFIG_SEND_FREQUENCY`); actual pkt/s limited by LabPSK AP replies (often lower)
- **Stall recovery (flash when board available):** `WIFI_PS_NONE`, CSI watchdog (restart ping ~8s, full Wi‑Fi/CSI recycle ~20s), TCP keepalive + force reconnect. Host ingest warns after ~15s idle.

## Later improvements (only when needed)

- Queue-drop metrics / backpressure
- Auth/TLS
- Live plot over TCP
- Avoid reflash when Mini IP changes (DHCP DNS or config another way)
- Board-stable `source_id` (STA MAC) instead of DHCP IP
- **Method 4.3 multi-RX:** 1× ESP sender + N× ESP receivers (ESP-NOW); Mini still fan-in on `:9055`; sender has no TCP

## Do not

- Run `--listen-tcp` on a laptop expecting data while C5 is flashed to the Mini IP
- Merge CSI + MediaMTX unless explicitly asked
- Treat LabPSK Wi‑Fi laptop reachability as required for capture (it is not)

## Espressif reference (remember)

Video: [ESP-CSI: Transforming Wi-Fi into a Sensing Platform](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JjdpzM6zVJ8) (Espressif Systems).

Key claims to keep in mind:
- CSI = pilots → environment-sensitive channel info (beyond RSSI); works NLOS / through walls
- No extra sensors — software on Wi‑Fi ESP (e.g. presence bulb)
- Demo: 1 TX + **8 RX** array for positioning (drone TX)
- **ESP32-C5** called out for higher sensitivity / 5.8 GHz; can sense tiny vibration / breathing-scale motion
- Gestures visible in raw CSI; on-device NN possible
- Vs mmWave/UWB: lower cost/power, wider range
- Accuracy: **fixed gain** (AGC can mask changes); multi-chip **co-crystal** sync for array / mm-level path disturbance
- Official path matches us: router CSI (method 4.1) + tools in [espressif/esp-csi](https://github.com/espressif/esp-csi)

Our lab priority stays: Mini TCP capture + interleaved presence labels. Arrays / fixed-gain / on-device NN / co-crystal = later upgrades, not blockers.
